 three of choice is nine related picks with a floor of three in each of Espionage and Military. The opening sentence prints +15% each for the three Espionage skills while the list prints Espionage: Any (+10%); the category holds one bonus, the list''s +10 is stored, and the further 5% on the three level-one Espionage picks is NOT stored; it is in the related note. Military is +15 in both places. Science: Math only is both Mathematics rows. Wilderness: Hunting is a catalog row with no percentage. No horsemanship: City troops are not trained to ride (printed 157). Cowboy: None is honoured by leaving the category out. Hand to Hand: Expert upgraded to Martial Arts or Assassin for one related skill; no alignment condition is printed for Assassin, so none is stored. || EQUIPMENT: the same paragraph as the Infantry Grunt; one weapon for each W.P. is four weapons of the player''s choice; a jacket, a full brimmed hat, a baseball cap, a web belt, a radio communicator with a 5 mile (8 km) range, a bedroll, an entrenching tool and the six reloads have no Rifts catalog row and are in GM Notes. Special-assignment issue (disguises, jump suits, camouflage, more armor, power armor, heavy weapons, explosives, vehicles) is in GM Notes. || MONEY: starts with 1D6x$1000 in personal savings (the text layer prints lD6x$1000); the monthly salary of $2600, +$250 per level, is in GM Notes."
