## Lore

Special Operations, the SO, are the special forces of the Tech-Cities. They
run the high security missions, from plain reconnaissance to black operations
deep in wilderness territory, and they are also allowed to work inside the
city as special investigators and internal defense against demonic invaders,
terrorists and other unusual threats. On the direct instruction of the City
Administration Office they may even spy on other government and corporate
departments.

They are tough, commando-style covert operatives: serious about their duty,
aggressive, fiercely loyal to their city, and often inclined to human
supremacy.

## GM Notes

Printed 96 says Special Operations answer only to the Military High Command
and the CAO, and that the SO and the Air Force are Melbourne''s strongest
departments. The City list on printed 105 says a City character met outside
the walls is an agent, an exile, a criminal, a rebel or a truant, unless the
whole group is a City team on assignment. Printed 105 also has SO task forces
guarding, and if need be killing, Administrators who hold sensitive secrets.

Spoken English is 86% plus 3D4%, rolled once; the sheet shows 86. The three
Espionage skills taken at level one are at +15%, 5% more than the sheet adds.

Kit beyond what the sheet lists (printed 125): a jacket, a full brimmed hat,
a baseball cap, a web belt, a radio communicator with a 5 mile (8 km) range,
a bedroll, an entrenching tool, and six reloads for the weapons. For special
assignments the SO may be issued disguises and undercover clothing, black
jump suits, camouflage suits, additional armor, power armor, heavy weapons,
explosives and vehicles, and they call on the Air Force for air support.

Pay: $2600 a month, +$250 per level of experience. Standard dormitory
housing, with private apartments for officers.
